Upstream: lavc/decode: change sw format selection logic in avcodec_default_get_format()
Commit:   3befae81f1dc (FFmpeg master, 2026-03-27)
Fixes:    https://trac.ffmpeg.org/ticket/7965

Backported onto FFmpeg 8.1.2, alongside hevc-alpha-videotoolbox.patch. Like
that one it landed on master after release/8.1 branched and was never
backported, so no 8.1.x point release carries it.

Second half of HEVC-with-alpha support. The hevc decoder offers get_format()
the alpha format first and the base-layer format last. Stock 8.1.2's
avcodec_default_get_format() returns the LAST software entry, so it always
picks the base-layer yuv420p and the alpha layer is never decoded -- upstream's
own commit message says the change "selects YUVA rather than YUV for HEVC with
alpha".

This is why the ffmpeg CLI already produced alpha without this patch while
ffprobe did not: ffmpeg CLI installs its own get_format callback that walks the
list front-to-back, which is exactly the logic this commit moves into the
default callback. Anything using the default -- ffprobe, and any libavcodec API
consumer -- needs this patch to decode the alpha layer at all.

Note this changes software format selection for every decoder, not just hevc.
Upstream made it unconditionally, and it aligns the default callback with the
CLI's long-standing behaviour, but it is the broadest of the three patches.

diff --git a/libavcodec/decode.c b/libavcodec/decode.c
--- a/libavcodec/decode.c
+++ b/libavcodec/decode.c
@@ -987,7 +987,6 @@ int avcodec_decode_subtitle2(AVCodecContext *avctx, AVSubtitle *sub,
 enum AVPixelFormat avcodec_default_get_format(struct AVCodecContext *avctx,
                                               const enum AVPixelFormat *fmt)
 {
-    const AVPixFmtDescriptor *desc;
     const AVCodecHWConfig *config;
     int i, n;
 
@@ -1014,12 +1013,13 @@ enum AVPixelFormat avcodec_default_get_format(struct AVCodecContext *avctx,
     // No device or other setup, so we have to choose from things which
     // don't any other external information.
 
-    // If the last element of the list is a software format, choose it
+    // Choose the first software format
     // (this should be best software format if any exist).
-    for (n = 0; fmt[n] != AV_PIX_FMT_NONE; n++);
-    desc = av_pix_fmt_desc_get(fmt[n - 1]);
-    if (!(desc->flags & AV_PIX_FMT_FLAG_HWACCEL))
-        return fmt[n - 1];
+    for (n = 0; fmt[n] != AV_PIX_FMT_NONE; n++) {
+        const AVPixFmtDescriptor *desc = av_pix_fmt_desc_get(fmt[n]);
+        if (!(desc->flags & AV_PIX_FMT_FLAG_HWACCEL))
+            return fmt[n];
+    }
 
     // Finally, traverse the list in order and choose the first entry
     // with no external dependencies (if there is no hardware configuration
diff --git a/libavcodec/decode.h b/libavcodec/decode.h
--- a/libavcodec/decode.h
+++ b/libavcodec/decode.h
@@ -111,8 +111,10 @@ int ff_set_sar(AVCodecContext *avctx, AVRational sar);
  * instead of calling get_format() directly.
  *
  * The list of pixel formats must contain at least one valid entry, and is
- * terminated with AV_PIX_FMT_NONE.  If it is possible to decode to software,
- * the last entry in the list must be the most accurate software format.
+ * terminated with AV_PIX_FMT_NONE. If it is possible to decode to software,
+ * the first entry after the last hwaccel one in the list must be the most
+ * accurate software format, followed by less accurate ones in order of
+ * preference.
  * If it is not possible to decode to software, AVCodecContext.sw_pix_fmt
  * must be set before calling this function.
  */
